{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["מפרסת פרסה — a single hoof like a kind of shoe, not claws on each toe like the hare and the hyrax." "ושסעת שסע — the hoof is split into two, not a single whole hoof like the horse and the donkey. And according to the plain sense of Scripture and the reply to the heretics: all the beasts, wild animals, birds, fish, kinds of locust, and creeping creatures that the Holy One, blessed be He, declared forbidden to Israel are repulsive and corrupt and heat up the body, and therefore they are called טמאים. And even authoritative physicians say so. And so too in the Talmud: gentiles who eat חגבים — their bodies are bruised." "מעלה גרה — brings its food up the gullet after eating."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {1 "The Aramaic phrase חבול גופייהו ('their bodies are bruised/swollen') appears in b. Avodah Zarah 37a in the context of gentiles eating forbidden creatures; עכו״ם expanded as עובדי כוכבים ומזלות."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:48:38.135264112Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}